//? Title: Depth-First Search: Actual Backtracking, First Paths and Complete Finish Times
//? Subtitle: Preserve recursive adjacency order with explicit frames, then measure events and stack depth
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a directed graph, a source and a target, we want to know whether a path
exists and return one if it does. Depth-first search follows one unseen
successor at a time, returning to an earlier vertex only after its current
branch is exhausted. The original two-vertex example is retained with visible
results. A seven-vertex control then shows genuine backtracking, a cycle
edge, early stopping and a first DFS path longer than the shortest path.
Native traces record discoveries, scanned original arcs, target states and
actual finishes without replay. Complete source traversal supplies valid
finish intervals, while explicit heap frames preserve the old recursive
order on a 200,000-vertex chain. We derive the reachable-work and linear
storage bounds, test adjacency-order effects, and distinguish active frames
from total graph/history memory.
)

\toc

> Keep the original path, then expose a backtracked branch

The original input, two vertices and the arc 0→1, returns [0,1], found=true
and expanded=2. Here expanded means first entries, including the goal; it
does not mean scanned edges. The larger prescribed graph has source zero
and goal six. Source adjacency is [1,2,6]. DFS first follows 0→1→3, scans
3→0 but finds zero already active, then finishes three and one. It resumes
zero at successor two and reaches the goal by 0→2→4→5→6 before inspecting
the direct arc 0→6. The diagram and transition table use actual native
records. Colours distinguish the returned path, the completed branch, the
active cycle edge and the unscanned direct alternative.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dfs_backtracking.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto original=dm::algorithms::depth_first_search(2,{{0,1}},0,1);
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1},{1,3},{3,0},{0,2},{2,4},{4,5},{5,6},{0,6}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,edges,0,6);const auto bfs=dm::algorithms::breadth_first_search(7,edges,0,6);
  if(original.path!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0,1} || t.result.path!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0,2,4,5,6} || t.events.size()!=17)return 1;
  std::vector<bool> on_path(7,false),scanned(edges.size(),false),back(edges.size(),false);
  for(auto v:t.result.path)on_path[v]=true;
  for(const auto& e:t.events)if(e.kind==dm::algorithms::DepthFirstEventKind::examine) {scanned[e.edge_index]=true;back[e.edge_index]=e.neighbor_state==dm::algorithms::DepthFirstState::active;}
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> positions{{0,0},{2,2},{2,-2},{4,2},{4,-2},{6,-2},{8,0}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(85,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.2;box.height=.9;box.font_size=20;
  for(std::size_t v=0;v<7;++v) {
    const bool done=t.state[v]==dm::algorithms::DepthFirstState::finished;box.fill=v==6?dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231}:done?dm::graphics::RGB{241,245,249}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
    d.node(std::to_string(v),positions[v],std::format("{}\n{}",v,v==6?"goal":done?"finished":"active"),box);
  }
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<edges.size();++i) {
    const auto [u,v]=edges[i];const bool tree=t.parent[v]==u&&t.parent_edge[v]==i;dm::graphics::DiagramStroke style;style.width=2;
    style.color=back[i]?dm::graphics::RGB{220,38,38}:tree&&on_path[u]&&on_path[v]?dm::graphics::RGB{22,163,74}:tree?dm::graphics::RGB{37,99,235}:dm::graphics::RGB{148,163,184};style.dashed=!scanned[i];
    d.edge(std::to_string(u),std::to_string(v),std::format("e{}{}",i,scanned[i]?"":" unscanned"),style);
  }
  d.text({4,3.5},"DFS finishes 3 and 1, resumes 0, then stops with its goal path active",22)
   .text({4,-3.4},std::format("DFS path {}; shortest-hop BFS path {}",t.result.path,bfs.path),21)
   .save_svg("build/dfs_backtracking.svg");
  std::print("Original control: path {}; found {}; expanded {}.\n\n",original.path,original.found,original.expanded);
  const std::vector<std::string> kinds{"discover","examine","finish","goal"},states{"unseen","active","finished"};
  std::print("| event | kind | vertex | neighbour | original edge | depth | active frames | target state before scan |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.events.size();++i) {
    const auto& e=t.events[i];const bool scan=e.kind==dm::algorithms::DepthFirstEventKind::examine;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,kinds[static_cast<std::size_t>(e.kind)],e.vertex,e.neighbor==7?"-":std::to_string(e.neighbor),e.edge_index==edges.size()?"-":std::to_string(e.edge_index),e.depth,e.stack_size,scan?states[static_cast<std::size_t>(e.neighbor_state)]:"-");
  }
  std::print("\nActual preorder {}; genuine postorder {}; scanned arcs {}; discovered {}; finished {}; maximum active frames {}.\n",t.preorder,t.postorder,t.work.edges_examined,t.work.discovered,t.work.finished,t.work.max_stack_size);
}
