\caption(Every reached vertex now has a genuine finish. Root zero encloses both completed branches, while vertex seven has no interval. Actual edge-target states distinguish six new-tree descents, two active-cycle arcs and two already-finished targets.)
\alttext(Seven horizontal intervals have integer discovery and finish ticks. Root zero spans zero through thirteen; its child intervals and their descendants nest. A separate row says vertex seven was unseen.)

For directed graphs, a scanned arc to an active vertex closes a cycle along
the ancestor path, including a self-loop. Arcs to finished vertices need not
cause descent; they may be forward or cross arcs. In a complete traversal of
a reachable DAG there are no active-target arcs, and reverse postorder is
a topological order of that reachable subgraph. This report's loop-containing
control is not claimed to have such an order. The API does not restart at
unseen vertices to construct a whole-graph DFS forest.

> Input order changes the first path and stopping work

The direct edge 0→6 exists in both larger goal-search runs. Move it from
last to first in source zero's adjacency and DFS returns [0,6], with two
entries and one scan. In the original order it returns a four-edge path
after seven entries and seven scans. BFS on that same graph returns the
one-edge path because it searches by hop distance. DFS's entry count is not
BFS's dequeue count; the table below compares DFS counts only. The unchanged
two-vertex control, unreachable target and start=goal cases make success and
empty/singleton path conventions explicit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dfs_order.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> original{{0,1},{1,3},{3,0},{0,2},{2,4},{4,5},{5,6},{0,6}};auto reordered=original;std::rotate(reordered.begin(),reordered.end()-1,reordered.end());
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::DepthFirstTrace> runs{
    dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(2,{{0,1}},0,1),dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,original,0,6),
    dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,reordered,0,6),dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(8,original,0,7),dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,original,0,0)};
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"original","late direct","direct first","unreachable","start=goal"};std::vector<double> x,entries;
  std::print("| case | found | returned path | entered vertices | scanned arcs | finished frames |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<runs.size();++k) {
    const auto& t=runs[k];x.push_back(k);entries.push_back(t.result.expanded);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",labels[k],t.result.found,t.result.path,t.result.expanded,t.work.edges_examined,t.work.finished);
  }
  if(runs[1].result.path.size()!=5 || runs[2].result.path!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0,6} || runs[3].result.found || runs[4].result.expanded!=1)return 1;
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars(x,entries,"vertex entries",{37,99,235},.6).legend({"vertex entries"},{{37,99,235}})
   .x_ticks(x,labels).title("The same direct arc can be reached early or late by DFS")
   .x_label("fixed directed search case").y_label("actual distinct first vertex entries")
   .x_limits(-.6,4.6).y_limits(0,9).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dfs_order.svg");
}
