> Linear trace work and worst-case active depth

For a completed source traversal, every reached vertex is discovered and
finished exactly once, and every outgoing adjacency entry of those vertices
is examined exactly once. There are therefore

\[
N_{\rm events}=2R+E_R.
\]
\alttext(Complete traversal retains two events per reached vertex and one per reachable adjacency entry.)

A successful goal run instead has R discoveries, F genuine finishes,
E_scan examinations and one goal event; its actual total is R+F+E_scan+1.
For the seven-vertex example, 7+2+7+1=17. A full tree has R=n and E_R=n−1,
so its trace has 3n−1 events regardless of branching shape. Active frames
are different: a chain reaches n, a binary tree grows logarithmically, and
a nontrivial star reaches two. The complete graph, state arrays and retained
history still use linear space in n+m even for a shallow tree. Explicit
frames remove recursive call-stack limits, not the need for memory.

Complete endpoint/terminal validation precedes adjacency allocation and all
optional caps, even for a trivial goal or bad unreachable arc. Trace limits
bound every original vertex and edge, including unreachable records, and
every actual retained event. Event caps are online; exhausting one throws
without a partial result. Zero disables only that optional cap, while
2n timestamp arithmetic and container capacities remain checked. The old
four-argument result function has no optional trace limits and allocates no
trace events. No external dataset is needed for these graph-order and work
controls; the reusable native tree generator supplies their exact inputs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dfs_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> sizes,events,theory,chain,binary,star;
  std::print("| vertices n | shape | discovered | finished | scanned tree arcs | events | 3n-1 | peak frames |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{8,16,32,64,128,256,512}) {
    const std::vector<std::size_t> branching{1,2,n};const std::vector<std::string> names{"chain","binary","star"};std::vector<double> peak;
    for(std::size_t k=0;k<branching.size();++k) {
      const auto t=dm::algorithms::depth_first_traversal(n,dm::algorithms::rooted_tree_edges(n,branching[k]),0);
      if(t.work.discovered!=n || t.work.finished!=n || t.work.edges_examined!=n-1 || t.events.size()!=3*n-1)return 1;
      peak.push_back(t.work.max_stack_size);if(k==0){sizes.push_back(n);events.push_back(t.events.size());theory.push_back(3*n-1);}
      if(n==8 || n==64 || n==512)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,names[k],t.work.discovered,t.work.finished,t.work.edges_examined,t.events.size(),3*n-1,t.work.max_stack_size);
    }
    chain.push_back(std::log2(peak[0]));binary.push_back(std::log2(peak[1]));star.push_back(std::log2(peak[2]));
  }
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> e{{0,1},{1,3},{3,0},{0,2},{2,4},{4,5},{5,6},{0,6}};int rejected=0;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,e,0,6,{6,8,17});}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,e,0,6,{7,7,17});}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,e,0,6,{7,8,16});}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,{{0,7}},0,0,{1,1,1});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,e,0,6,{7,8,17}),disabled=dm::algorithms::depth_first_search_trace(7,e,0,6,{0,0,0});
  const auto deep=dm::algorithms::depth_first_search(200000,dm::algorithms::rooted_tree_edges(200000,1),0,199999);
  if(rejected!=4 || exact.events.size()!=17 || disabled.events.size()!=17 || !deep.found || deep.path.size()!=200000)return 1;
  std::print("\nFour expected rejections: vertex cap, complete edge cap, actual event cap, invalid endpoint before trivial-goal/cap checks. Count {}. Exact 7/8/17 limits and zero-disabled optional caps succeed.\n",rejected);
  std::print("Deep chain: entered {}; returned path vertices {}; first {}; last {}.\n",deep.expanded,deep.path.size(),deep.path.front(),deep.path.back());
  auto work=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();work.line(sizes,events,"actual",{37,99,235},2).points(sizes,theory,"3n-1",{31,41,55},4)
    .legend({"actual","3n-1"},{{37,99,235},{31,41,55}}).title("Full traversal: 3n - 1 events").x_label("vertices n").y_label("retained actual events").x_limits(0,550).y_limits(0,1900);
  auto space=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();space.line(sizes,chain,"chain",{37,99,235},2).line(sizes,binary,"binary",{234,88,12},2).line(sizes,star,"star",{31,41,55},2)
    .legend({"chain","binary","star"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12},{31,41,55}}).title("Active depth, logarithmic scale").x_label("vertices n").y_label("log2(maximum active frames)").x_limits(0,550).y_limits(0,11);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(work).add(space).size(1100,520).title("Linear event counts and worst-case active depth").fit_panels().save_svg("build/dfs_work.svg");
}
